{
  "$comment": [
    "G5 (0.3.78) single source for the family's cross-file FACTS.",
    "A fact here is a statement that used to live in two or more tracked documents and",
    "therefore drifted (0.3.77: the root README still claimed that sessions on other",
    "presets keep the shared automation, and the agent README still claimed there is no",
    "cordis base after bases.json grew one).",
    "Rules of the table: every fact has exactly ONE home document; other documents CITE",
    "the home (the `cites` entries) instead of restating it; a `must` entry marked",
    "unique may appear in the home ONLY - a second copy anywhere in the tracked docs",
    "fails verify-arch-guards rule N19. `machine` entries re-derive the statement from",
    "the code/data that owns the value, so a changed value with a stale doc also fails.",
    "Version history (CHANGELOG.md) is the REASON layer and is exempt from `forbid`: a",
    "released version section records what was true then and is never rewritten.",
    "packages/docs/** is gitignored (not a versionable surface): it may be a source of",
    "material, never a home; the lib skips it by name."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "scan": {
    "repoDocs": [
      "README.md",
      "README.zh.md",
      "INSTALL.md",
      "CHANGELOG.md",
      "CONTRIBUTING.md"
    ],
    "reasonLayer": [
      "CHANGELOG.md"
    ],
    "treeDocSkip": [
      "node_modules",
      "lib",
      "dist",
      "docs",
      ".release-staging",
      ".release-staging.next",
      ".release-staging.previous",
      "dist.next",
      ".git"
    ]
  },
  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "service-key-prefix",
      "title": "the family's own service keys: one prefix, two registered exceptions",
      "home": "README.md",
      "machine": {
        "kind": "service-key-prefix",
        "prefix": "evolution",
        "exceptions": [
          {
            "key": "memory",
            "reason": "the key predates the prefix rule and family readers reach it through ctx.memory",
            "expiry": "group 6 (O-3): rename behind an alias window, or keep the registration"
          },
          {
            "key": "skillUsage",
            "reason": "same shape: a historical generic key with in-family readers",
            "expiry": "group 6 (O-3): rename behind an alias window, or keep the registration"
          }
        ]
      },
      "must": [
        {
          "text": "**every key is prefixed `evolution`**"
        },
        {
          "text": "`memory`"
        },
        {
          "text": "`skillUsage`"
        }
      ],
      "forbid": [],
      "cites": []
    },
    {
      "id": "skill-name-home",
      "title": "which name a skill is published under: the directory name, and the open decision",
      "home": "evolution-skill-catalog/README.md",
      "machine": {
        "kind": "skill-name-home",
        "file": "evolution-core/src/frontmatter.ts",
        "marker": "if (expectedName && parsed.frontmatter.name !== expectedName)"
      },
      "must": [
        {
          "text": "The family's canonical name for a skill is its **directory name**."
        },
        {
          "text": "**Decision 1 is open**",
          "unique": true
        }
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "re": "the family publishes the frontmatter name",
          "why": "the validator refuses a frontmatter name that differs from the target, and the provider publishes the scanned (directory) name — a document may not claim the opposite"
        }
      ],
      "cites": []
    },
    {
      "id": "event-mode",
